{
  "delta_from_prior": "Compared to neon_worstcase_auto_00055 (18 vars, 204 clauses, which compressed to width-5 near-parity blocks and was refuted at root by IALH-5 with peak 0), this fixture uses width-6 non-affine quotient blocks (lifted to width-8 blocks on 16 vars, 456 clauses) so root IALH-5 derives zero conflicts/constraints. Compared to Neon53 (16 vars, 408 clauses, 1 extra quotient point / 4 lifted points per block, which achieved peak 16 on v3 but was defeated by the experimental delta<=4 core repair), this fixture places 3 opposite-parity quotient points (12 lifted points) in each block, preserving odd quotient cardinality (19, trivial stabilizer), v3 compression (16->12), and peak-16 residual search while provably defeating delta<=4 core repair on every block. Compared to fable_worstcase_auto_00059 (32 vars, 128 clauses, inconclusive DPLL oracle timeout), this 16-var fixture stays fast for the independent bounded DPLL oracle.",
  "explanation": "### Audit of Pinned v3 (`blq-localcert-scc-emra-ialh5-v3`)\nNo soundness bug (wrong SAT answer) is claimed. The v3 local-certificate verifier checks every local block assignment, enforces block-supported forms, partitions quotient clauses across blocks, verifies `P * L = I` entrywise, and falls back to exact search on any failure. Combined with the Lean-checked semantic core (`FibreCardinality.binary_block_certificate` and `counted_blocks_equisatisfiable`), the preprocessing step is sound.\n\nThe verified vulnerability is **post-compression residual search growth** on a formula where v3 compression **succeeds** (not a discovery skip), and where the resulting quotient defeats root Canon, signed SCC, IALH-5, DP, and also defeats the experimental `delta <= 4` core repair.\n\n### Construction (16 Variables, 456 Clauses, Width 8)\nPartition the 16 variables into four interleaved 4-variable groups:\n- `G1 = (1, 5, 9, 13)`, parity `u1 = x1 ^ x5 ^ x9 ^ x13`\n- `G2 = (2, 6, 10, 14)`, parity `u2 = x2 ^ x6 ^ x10 ^ x14`\n- `G3 = (3, 7, 11, 15)`, parity `u3 = x3 ^ x7 ^ x11 ^ x15`\n- `G4 = (4, 8, 12, 16)`, parity `u4 = x4 ^ x8 ^ x12 ^ x16`\n\nStart from a 6-clause UNSAT 2-SAT base on `(u1, u2, u3, u4)` using all 6 distinct pairs:\n1. `(-u1 v u2)` on `(G1, G2)`: forbids `(u1=1, u2=0)`\n2. `(-u2 v u3)` on `(G2, G3)`: forbids `(u2=1, u3=0)`\n3. `(-u3 v -u1)` on `(G1, G3)`: forbids `(u1=1, u3=1)`\n4. `(u1 v u4)` on `(G1, G4)`: forbids `(u1=0, u4=0)`\n5. `(-u4 v u2)` on `(G2, G4)`: forbids `(u2=0, u4=1)`\n6. `(-u3 v -u4)` on `(G3, G4)`: forbids `(u3=1, u4=1)`\n\nUNSAT check: `u1=1 => u2=1 => u3=1`, contradicting (3); `u1=0 => u4=1 => u2=1 => u3=1`, contradicting (6). Lifting each binary clause to width 8 yields 6 exact-support blocks of 64 clauses each (`384` base clauses), which is UNSAT.\n\n### Exact Perturbation Clauses (72 Extra Clauses, 12 per Block)\nIn each block `k` forbidding `(u_i, u_j) = (a_k, b_k)`, we add 12 extra width-8 clauses obtained by lifting **3 distinct quotient points** in the opposite-parity coset `(1-a_k, 1-b_k)` under the quotient map `y_1..y_8 = x_1..x_8`, `y_9 = x_9^x_13`, `y_10 = x_10^x_14`, `y_11 = x_11^x_15`, `y_12 = x_12^x_16`. Specifically, letting `E1, E2` be the first two even-parity cosets `{(0,0,0,0),(0,0,1,1)}` and `{(0,1,0,1),(0,1,1,0)}`, and `O1, O2` be the first two odd-parity cosets `{(0,0,0,1),(0,0,1,0)}` and `{(0,1,0,0),(0,1,1,1)}` on each group, each block adds `(C_i1 x C_j1) U (C_i2 x C_j1) U (C_i1 x C_j2)` of parity `(1-a_k, 1-b_k)` (`4 + 4 + 4 = 12` clauses per block, `76` clauses/block, `456` total). Adding clauses preserves UNSAT and speeds up the independent bounded DPLL oracle.\n\n### Discovery Succeeds; Residual Growth Follows\n1. **Exact v3 Compression (16 vars / 456 clauses -> 12 vars / 114 clauses)**: Each block's quotient forbidden set has cardinality `16 + 3 = 19` (odd), so its quotient stabilizer is trivial `{0}`. Thus each lifted width-8 block has exact 2-dimensional stabilizer `K_k = span{e_{8+i}^e_{12+i}, e_{8+j}^e_{12+j}}`. All 6 annihilators are compatible and spanned by the 8 weight-1 forms `x_1..x_8` and 4 weight-2 forms `x_9^x_13, x_10^x_14, x_11^x_15, x_12^x_16`, each occurring in 3 blocks. Greedy basis selection accepts all 12 forms, compresses to 12 variables / 114 clauses (6 width-6 blocks of 19 clauses), and passes exact equivalence verification (including Lean).\n2. **Root IALH-5 Blindness**: Every quotient block has width `6 > 5`. For any window `W` with `|W| <= 5`: if `W` is not contained in a single block, every block has `>= 2` unassigned variables and zero UP triggers; if `W` lies inside one block `B_k`, flipping the 6th variable changes only one group's parity, so the two completions can never hit both `(a_k, b_k)` and `(1-a_k, 1-b_k)` (hence no direct conflict), and any forced 6th variable leaves all 6 variables in the other two groups unassigned, so every other block still has `>= 3` unassigned variables and UP halts. Thus root IALH-5 derives zero conflicts and zero constraints.\n3. **Root DP Rejection & Peak-16 Search**: Every quotient variable has `>= 24` positive and `>= 24` negative occurrences across 3 blocks, so DP rejects all eliminations at root. Because the 4 groups are interleaved in ascending quotient order (`y_1..y_4` hit `G1..G4` once each), branching reaches depth 4 (`2 / 4 / 8 / 16` open branches, peak `>= 16`) with every group still having 2 unassigned variables and every block still width 4 before DP/refutation closes depth 5.\n\n### Defeating Experimental Core Repair & Challenging Fable's Proposals\nOn each lifted block (`m = 76`), the 12 extra points form 3 cosets `C1, C2, C3` of `K_k`. For any `v` outside `K_k`, `count(v) <= 24` if `v` is outside the base stabilizer `S_0`, and `count(v) <= 64 + 8 = 72 = m - 4` if `v in S_0 \\ K_k` (attained simultaneously by all three coset differences `v_12, v_13, v_23`). Thus `delta = 0..3` finds no vector outside `K_k`, while `delta = 4` keeps all three differences simultaneously, whose span with `K_k` has size `16 > 12`, forcing removal of all 12 extra points, which exceeds the `<= 4` removal cap. Hence experimental core repair rejects every `delta in 0..4` and cannot reduce the instance to 2-SAT.\n\nThis also directly challenges Fable's untrusted fibre-transfer / bounded-gap / collapse-rank proposals: fixed-`delta` or small-gap affine repair is defeated by an `O(1)` opposite-parity perturbation (3 quotient points) while keeping exact BLQ compression active, and without a theorem controlling residual branching after nonlinear/perturbed quotients, local compression alone does not bound total solver work.",
